# Day 3 - AI Travel Assistant: Prompt Testing and Evaluation

## Objective
Build an AI-powered travel assistant, evaluate its responses,
improve the system prompt, and analyze temperature settings.

## Business
TripWise Travel Services is a demonstration travel business
that provides domestic travel packages and customer assistance.

## Technologies Used
- Python
- Google Colab
- Groq API
- LangChain
- GPT-OSS-120B
- CSV

## Features
- Business-specific system prompt
- Dynamic business details using Python dictionaries
- Automated testing with 10 customer questions
- Keyword-based response evaluation
- Prompt improvement and performance comparison
- Temperature-based response analysis
- Agent and non-agent task classification

## Experimental Results

| Experiment | Temperature | Passed | Pass Rate |
|------------|-------------|--------|-----------|
| Original Prompt | 0 | 4/10 | 40% |
| Improved Prompt | 0 | 8/10 | 80% |
| Run 1 | 1.0 | 9/10 | 90% |
| Run 2 | 1.0 | 7/10 | 70% |

## Prompt Improvement
Added an instruction to preserve exact words, numerical
values, and time formats from the business facts.

The observed pass rate increased from 40% to 80%,
an improvement of 40 percentage points.

## Temperature Analysis
At temperature 1.0, two runs produced different pass
rates of 90% and 70%, demonstrating response variability.

These are observed results from the initial experiments.
Results may vary in subsequent executions.

## Agent or Not

| Business Task | Classification |
|---------------|----------------|
| Calculate travel package cost | Plain Code |
| Answer customer questions | One LLM Call |
| Dynamically plan a personalized trip | Agent |

## Files
- task.py - Python implementation
- tests.csv - Customer questions and expected keywords
- README.md - Project documentation

## How to Run

1. Install the required library:

   pip install langchain-groq

2. Run the Python script:

   python task.py

3. Enter your Groq API key when prompted, if not configured.

## Conclusion
This experiment demonstrates how prompt engineering,
automated testing, and temperature settings influence
LLM responses.

Keyword-based evaluation does not guarantee complete
answer correctness. Agent classification is conceptual;
a tool-calling agent is not implemented in this task.
